==Introduction==

===Abstract===

This document proposes a standard for the NestedMuSig2 multi-signature scheme
introduced in [[https://eprint.iacr.org/2026/223|Kohen (2026)]]. NestedMuSig2 is
a recursive variant of [[bip-0327.mediawiki|BIP327]] (MuSig2) in which the
public key of any participant in a signing group may itself be a MuSig2
aggregate key, allowing a tree of nested cosigner groups to collaboratively
produce a single [[bip-0340.mediawiki|BIP340]]-compatible Schnorr signature.

The output is a standard 64-byte BIP340 signature that verifies under a standard
32-byte x-only aggregate public key. The resulting signature is
indistinguishable on-chain from a single-signer Taproot key-path spend and can
be verified using ordinary BIP340 verification using only the aggregate x-only
public key, without revealing or requiring knowledge of the underlying signer
set or Taproot script tree. The scheme supports [[bip-0032.mediawiki|BIP32]] key
derivation and [[bip-0341.mediawiki|BIP341]] Taproot tweaking, and is compatible
with existing protocols that consume MuSig2 outputs.

